# shapelock — harmonics INSIDE a cell (3 axes, closed triangle)
# (a/b)(b/c)(c/a) = 1 identically: closure, not a constraint.
# volume fixed (x+y+z=0), so only SHAPE moves — the constant-
# volume soft mode a scalar radius does not have.

== S1. THE SHAPE SPECTRUM (exact integer enumeration) ==
admissible = integer triple (a:b:c), gcd 1, with ALL THREE
pairwise ratios at Tenney height <= ceiling. No solver here, so
this section cannot be a search artifact.
 ceiling   n_shapes(<=12)  n_shapes(<=32)   first few
       0               1               1   1:1:1 
       1               3               3   1:1:1 1:1:2 1:2:2 
       2               8               8   1:1:1 1:1:2 1:1:3 1:1:4 1:2:2 
       3              26              26   1:1:1 1:1:2 1:1:3 1:1:4 1:1:5 
       4              64              95   1:1:1 1:1:2 1:1:3 1:1:4 1:1:5 
       5             113             291   1:1:1 1:1:2 1:1:3 1:1:4 1:1:5 
       6             189             538   1:1:1 1:1:2 1:1:3 1:1:4 1:1:5 
       7             275            1061   1:1:1 1:1:2 1:1:3 1:1:4 1:1:5 
       8             287            2026   1:1:1 1:1:2 1:1:3 1:1:4 1:1:5 

reading: a spectrum that GROWS with the ceiling but stays small
and enumerable is a shape quantisation. If it explodes, the comb
selects nothing; if it stays at 1 (the sphere), it forbids shape.

== S2. DOES SHAPE LOCK UNDER SHEAR? ==
Pure deviatoric load sigma = t*(2,-1,-1)/3 (volume preserved).
comb_limit=4, s=0.05, lam=0.10. Rung-seeded exhaustive search.
